  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot Auktion Facility for Methan and Climate Change Mitigation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the Pilot Auction Facility for Methane and Climate Change Mitigation (PAF), the World Bank launched an innovative fund. Based on the concept of result-based payments, which were based on the independent review and the approval process of the Framework Convention on Climate Change with public participation, cost-effective greenhouse gas emission reductions were to be ensured. The funds deposited were used via an auction process that promoted competition among providers and thus avoided deadweight effects. The fund was aimed at CDM projects that were wholly or essentially dependent on the sale of international certificates (CER, certified emission reductions) and which, in view of insufficient market demand for certificates, could not continue their emission reduction activities.</narrative>
  </description>
